               </text>
            </section>
            <section>
               <title value="Hospital course note"/>
               <code>
                  <coding>
                     <system value="http://loinc.org"/>
                     <code value="8648-8"/>
                     <display value="Hospital course note"/>
                  </coding>
               </code>
               <text>
                  <status value="generated"/>
                  <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Dear Colleague, I am writing to inform you regarding your patient, an 85-year-old male admitted on 11/06/1998 with an acute exacerbation of known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, the patient presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Clinical examination confirmed diminished air entry with widespread expiratory wheeze. Chest X-ray showed hyperinflation without evidence of pneumonia or pneumothorax. Arterial blood gas analysis revealed hypoxaemia with mild hypercapnia. Blood tests showed elevated inflammatory markers. The patient was treated with nebulised bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, supplemental oxygen therapy, and intravenous fluids. He responded well to treatment with gradual improvement in respiratory function and oxygen saturation. He is discharged home with oral prednisolone taper and optimised inhaler regimen. Please arrange follow-up within two weeks. Do not hesitate to contact me should you require further information.</div>
               </text>
            </section>
